    "articleEn": "{{Greenhouse}} gases are causing a {{phenomenon}} known as climate change, which has the potential to bring about {{calamity}} and {{catastrophic}} consequences. The effects of this {{destructive}} process are already being felt in various parts of the world, with extreme weather events becoming more frequent and severe.\n\nOne example of such an event is {{El Niño}}, a warming of the ocean surface that occurs every few years and can cause droughts and floods in different regions. These changes in weather patterns can {{endanger}} the lives and livelihoods of people and animals alike.\n\nHuman activities that release large amounts of greenhouse gases, such as burning fossil fuels and deforestation, {{jeopardise}} the future of our planet. If we do not take action to reduce our carbon footprint, we risk facing even more severe consequences in the future.\n\nWe must also be aware of the potential for {{mishap}} in our daily lives. A small {{pebble}} on the road can cause a car accident, and a loose {{magnet}} can cause injury if swallowed. By taking small precautions and being aware of our surroundings, we can prevent such accidents from occurring.\n\nIn conclusion, it is important to recognize the impact that our actions can have on the environment and on ourselves. By being mindful of the {{destructive}} effects of climate change and taking steps to reduce our carbon footprint, we can avoid potential {{calamity}} and protect the future of our planet.",
    "articleZh": "温室气体正在引起一种被称为气候变化的现象，这可能会带来灾难和灾难性的后果。这种破坏性过程的影响已经在世界各地的一些地区感受到，极端天气事件变得更加频繁和严重。\n\n其中一个例子是厄尔尼诺，这是海洋表面变暖的现象，每隔几年就会发生，可能在不同地区引发干旱和洪水。这种天气模式的变化可能会危及人和动物的生命和生计。\n\n释放大量温室气体的人类活动，例如燃烧化石燃料和砍伐森林，危及我们星球的未来。如果我们不采取行动来减少碳足迹，我们将面临更严重的后果。\n\n我们还必须意识到我们日常生活中发生意外事故的潜在可能性。路上的一个小鹅卵石可以导致车祸，一个松动的磁铁如果吞下会导致伤害。通过采取小的预防措施并注意我们的周围环境，我们可以防止这些意外事件的发生。\n\n总之，认识到我们的行为对环境和我们自己的影响非常重要。通过注意气候变化的破坏性影响并采取措施减少我们的碳足迹，我们可以避免潜在的灾难，并保护我们星球的未来。",
