    "articleEn": "Theme: A scientific look at how plants survive and adapt.\n\nIf you pick up a book on {{botany}}, you will quickly realize that a plant is not just a simple object. It is a complex, living {{organism}} that works like a factory. The most famous process in this factory is {{photosynthesis}}. During the day, plants use {{sunlight}} to create {{energy}}. They {{absorb}} carbon {{dioxide}} from the air and {{release}} fresh oxygen for us to breathe. However, many people do not know that plants also {{respire}}, taking in oxygen to stay alive, just like animals do.\n\nInside the plant, there is a busy system of {{circulation}}. The roots ensure the {{uptake}} of water and key {{nutrients}} from the soil. To help process this food, the plant uses a special {{mechanism}} involving {{enzymes}}. An {{enzyme}} acts as a {{catalyst}}, making chemical reactions happen faster so the plant can grow strong.\n\nBut why do plants look so different? The answer lies in {{genetics}}. Over millions of years, plants {{evolve}} to fit their {{surroundings}}. Sometimes, a random {{mutation}} occurs in a seed. This leads to a {{variation}} in color or shape. This process creates the incredible {{diversity}} of {{vegetation}} we see today.\n\nScientists try to {{classify}} these plants into groups. You might study a small {{herb}} used in medicine, or a strong {{perennial}} tree that survives for centuries. In modern farming, scientists use {{hybridisation}} to mix species and {{reproduce}} better crops. However, we must be careful. Every plant is part of a delicate {{ecosystem}}. To protect our {{ecology}}, we should try to be {{eco-friendly}}. We must respect the {{environment}} that supports all life.",
    "articleZh": "主题： 用科学的眼光看待植物如何生存与适应。\n\n翻开一本植物学书籍，你很快就会意识到，植物绝非简单的物体。它是一个复杂的、有生命的有机体，运作起来就像一座工厂。这座工厂里最著名的工序就是光合作用。白天，植物利用阳光制造能量。它们从空气中吸收二氧化碳，并释放出清新的氧气供我们呼吸。然而，许多人不知道植物也会呼吸，就像动物一样，它们也需要摄入氧气来维持生命。\n\n在植物内部，有一个繁忙的循环系统。根部确保从土壤中摄取水分和关键的营养物质。为了处理这些食物，植物使用一种涉及酶的特殊机制。酶充当催化剂，加速化学反应，从而使植物长得壮实。\n\n但为什么植物看起来千差万别呢？答案在于遗传学。经过数百万年的演变，植物不断进化以适应其环境（surroundings）。有时，种子中会发生随机突变。这导致了颜色或形状的变异。正是这一过程创造了我们今天所见的植被惊人的多样性。\n\n科学家试图将这些植物分类。你可能会研究一种用于入药的小草本植物，或者一棵存活几个世纪的强壮的多年生植物。在现代农业中，科学家利用杂交技术混合物种并繁殖出更好的作物。然而，我们必须小心。每一种植物都是脆弱的生态系统的一部分。为了保护我们的生态，我们应该努力做到对生态环境友好。我们必须尊重维持所有生命的环境（environment）。",
