    "articleEn": "Theme: A team of scientists welcomes visitors and protects the valley’s animals.\n\nSara was a young {{biologist}} who worked at a famous research reserve. Her small team studied all kinds of {{wildlife}}. Elena was a skilled {{botanist}} who cataloged the valley’s rare {{flora}}, while Marcus was a dedicated {{zoologist}} studying the local {{fauna}}. Together with an experienced {{ecologist}} named Tom, they worked day and night to protect every living {{creature}} in the valley.\n\nOne sunny morning, a large {{crowd}} gathered outside the center’s gates. Soon, a curious {{throng}} moved into the main hall to hear the morning lecture. Sara stood beside a giant diagram of life. “Every {{species}} on Earth has a deep history,” she told the visitors. “Many modern animals {{originate}} in prehistoric waters. In fact, most living forms {{derive}} their core body plans from a common {{ancestor}}. Many physical differences {{stem}} from changes in environment over millions of years.”\n\nMarcus pointed to several skeletons to explain comparative {{anatomy}}. “As you can see, every {{vertebrate}} has a backbone,” he said. He showed how each {{offspring}} inherits a tiny {{gene}} from its parents, shaping every future {{descendant}}. He explained that a cold-blooded {{reptile}} and a wet-skinned {{amphibian}} represent older lineages. Higher branches include each furry {{mammal}} and agile {{primate}}, which often forms a distinct {{subgroup}} on the family tree.\n\nNext, Tom explained animal roles in nature. A fierce {{carnivore}} hunts for fresh food, while a peaceful {{herbivore}} feeds on trees and grass. He looked out the window and pointed to the meadows. The visitors watched a majestic {{herd}} of deer resting by the river, while a noisy {{flock}} of birds flew across the sky, and a dense {{swarm}} of wild bees buzzed around blooming flowers.\n\nSuddenly, an alarm rang near the valley fence. A greedy hunter, a local {{brute}} known for his {{cruel}} traps, was trying to capture a magnificent mountain {{beast}}. The team acted quickly with the rangers and chased the man away before any animal was hurt. The valley was peaceful once again, and the visitors learned how precious each life truly is.",
    "articleZh": "主题： 一组科学家接待访客并保护山谷中的动物。\n\n萨拉是一位年轻的生物学家，在一家著名的保护区研究站工作。她的小团队研究各种野生动物。埃莱娜是一位熟练的植物学家，负责记录山谷中珍稀的植物群，而马库斯是一位敬业的动物学家，专门研究当地的动物群。再加上一位名叫汤姆的经验丰富的生态学家，他们日以继夜地工作，以保护山谷中的每一种生物。\n\n一个阳光明媚的早晨，大批人群聚集在研究中心的大门外。很快，好奇的人群涌入大厅聆听早间讲座。萨拉站在一幅巨大的生命图谱旁。“地球上的每一个物种都有一段深厚的历史，”她告诉访客们。“许多现代动物发源于史前水域。事实上，大多数生命形态都源自同一个共同祖先的基本身体构造。许多外形差异则源于数百万年来环境的变迁。”\n\n马库斯指着几副骨骼来解释比较解剖学。“正如大家所见，每一种脊椎动物都有一根脊柱，”他说。他展示了每一个后代如何从父母那里继承微小的基因，从而塑造未来的每一个后代。他解释说，冷血的爬行动物和湿皮的两栖动物代表了更古老的谱系。更高的分支包括每一种长毛的哺乳动物和敏捷的灵长动物，后者在生命之树上通常形成一个独特的子群。\n\n接着，汤姆解释了动物在自然界中的角色。凶猛的肉食动物捕猎新鲜食物，而温和的食草动物则以树叶和青草为食。他望向窗外，指着草地。游客们看到一群威严的鹿在河边休息，一群喧闹的鸟儿飞过天空，还有一群密集的野蜂在盛开的花丛周围嗡嗡作响。\n\n突然，山谷围栏附近警报大作。一个贪婪的猎人，一个因设置残忍的陷阱而闻名的当地残忍的人，正试图捕捉一只雄伟的山地野兽。团队迅速与护林员一起行动，在动物受伤前将那个人赶跑了。山谷再次恢复了平静，访客们也真正体会到了每一个生命的珍贵。",
