    "articleEn": "Theme: People can protect animals by understanding their habits and caring for their homes.\n\nLeo was an animal {{keeper}} at a green valley reserve, while his friend Dan was an old {{shepherd}} who lived by simple {{subsistence}} farming. Together, they worked hard so wild beasts and farm animals could peacefully {{exist}} in the same mountain {{habitat}}. Recently, a scary winter illness arrived, and Leo was worried about an {{epidemic}}. A deadly {{virus}} or dangerous {{bacteria}} could spread quickly through the herds. Even a tiny {{germ}} or invisible {{microbe}} could make any weak creature a helpless {{victim}}.\n\nIn early spring, many forest animals {{undergo}} big changes. Some had remained {{dormant}} during their long winter {{hibernation}}, but now they began to wake up. Across the hills, a guard dog would {{bark}} to warn strangers, and a distant lion would {{roar}} in the wind. Leo loved studying their natural {{behaviour}}. Under the stones, beetles would {{crawl}}, and small spiders would {{creep}} through dead leaves. In the trees, birds gathered twigs for each new {{nest}}, while bees worked inside a wild {{hive}}, filling every tiny wax {{cell}} with honey.\n\nTo keep the valley safe, Leo had to {{track}} animals that left only a light foot {{trace}} in the mud. He used an {{optical}} camera to see far into the valley and an {{acoustic}} device to hear faint sounds. Because many hunters were {{nocturnal}}, he worked late into the night. Leo had great {{intelligence}} and an {{intuitive}} feeling for nature. He believed every wounded creature had the {{potential}} to heal and return to the forest. Their bodies were fast and {{flexible}}, and their ears were extremely {{sensitive}}.\n\nDanger was never far away. A hungry {{predator}} would always search for easy {{prey}}. Dan’s young lambs were especially {{vulnerable}} at night. However, Dan did not want to {{exterminate}} the mountain wolves. Instead, the men built a thick thorny {{hedge}} and a solid wooden {{barrier}}. Dan checked every metal {{bar}} along the fence. He kept his horses inside a warm {{stable}} and stored his winter food inside the dry {{barn}}.\n\nSometimes Leo had to treat an injured beast as a temporary {{captive}}. He put it in a spacious {{cage}} that was clean and {{functional}}. He understood wild {{instinct}} very well. When an animal was frightened, it showed {{defensive}} actions; it might try to {{bite}} with sharp teeth, just as a bee might {{sting}} if disturbed. Leo never tried to {{tame}} these wild patients. Instead, he would softly {{rub}} healing oil on a wound so the beast would not {{suffer}}.\n\nTo stay alert, Leo and Dan would {{alternate}} watches between the farm and the forest. By respecting nature’s rules, the two men kept the valley safe and healthy for every living thing.",
    "articleZh": "主题： 人类可以通过了解动物的习性并关爱它们的家园来保护动物。\n\n利奥是一处绿谷保护区的动物饲养员，而他的朋友丹则是一位靠简单的自给自足农业为生的老牧羊人。他们共同努力，以便野生野兽和农场牲畜能和平地共存在同一片山区栖息地。最近，一种可怕的冬季疾病悄然来袭，利奥十分担心会爆发流行病。致命的病毒或危险的细菌可能在畜群中迅速蔓延。哪怕是微小的病菌或隐形的微生物，都能让任何虚弱的生灵沦为无助的受害者。\n\n在初春，许多森林动物都会经历巨大的变化。有些在漫长的冬季冬眠中一直保持休眠状态，但现在它们开始苏醒了。漫山遍野间，看门狗会吠叫以警告陌生人，远处的狮子也会在风中怒吼。利奥非常喜欢研究它们的自然行为。石头底下，甲虫在爬行，小蜘蛛在枯叶间潜行。树林中，鸟儿为每一个新巢收集树枝，蜜蜂则在野生的蜂巢内辛勤劳作，用蜂蜜填满每一个小小的蜡质蜂房。\n\n为了守护山谷的安全，利奥必须追踪那些在泥地里只留下浅浅足迹的动物。他使用光学相机远眺山谷深处，并用声学设备去聆听微弱的声响。因为许多捕食者都是夜间活动的，所以他工作到深夜。利奥拥有极高的智慧和对自然的直觉感知。他相信每一只受伤的生灵都有潜能康复并重返森林。它们的身体敏捷而灵活，耳朵也极其灵敏。\n\n危险从未远离。饥饿的捕食者总是在寻觅容易得手的猎物。丹的幼崽羊羔在夜晚尤其脆弱。然而，丹并不想去消灭山里的狼群。相反，这两个人筑起了一道茂密多刺的树篱和坚固的木制屏障。丹仔细检查了沿篱笆分布的每一根金属栏杆。他把马匹关在温暖的马厩里，并将过冬的粮食储存在干燥的谷仓内。\n\n有时，利奥不得不将受伤的野兽作为临时的圈养动物进行医治。他将其安置在一个宽敞、干净且实用的笼子里。他非常理解野生的本能。当动物受惊时，会表现出防御性的举动；它可能会试图用锋利的牙齿去咬人，就像蜜蜂受到打扰时会蜇人一样。利奥从未试图去驯化这些野生病患。相反，他会轻柔地在伤口上涂抹具有疗效的药油，这样野兽就不会感到痛苦。\n\n为了保持警惕，利奥和丹在农场和森林之间交替巡逻。通过遵循大自然的法则，这两个人让山谷对每一个生命来说都保持着安全与健康。",
