    "articleEn": "Theme: Looking at the sky helps scientists discover the secrets of the universe.\n\nToby worked late at night at the mountain {{observatory}}. From a young age, he dreamed of becoming an {{astronaut}} and traveling into the vast {{cosmos}}. Instead, he chose to study real science and became a researcher in {{astronomy}}. Sometimes his friends teased him about reading horoscopes, but he always explained that science had nothing to do with {{astrology}}. To Toby, the entire {{universe}} was full of real mysteries waiting to be understood.\n\nTonight was special. Toby pointed a large {{telescope}} into the dark sky to watch a famous {{comet}}. As it moved along its ancient {{orbit}}, it passed close to the plane of the {{ecliptic}}. A glowing {{envelope}} of gas and space {{dust}} wrapped around its head, creating a bright tail. Looking deeper, Toby could also see a distant spiral {{galaxy}} shining far away. It was a true {{celestial}} {{spectacle}} that filled his heart with wonder.\n\nSuddenly, his colleague Nina came into the lab carrying a heavy box. She had just returned from a dry desert valley where a huge circular {{crater}} sat in the ground. Inside the box was a dark, heavy {{chunk}} of rock covered in gray {{ash}}. “I collected this {{sample}} near the impact site,” Nina said excitedly. “We need to check whether it is an {{interstellar}} rock from deep space or just normal {{terrestrial}} stone.”\n\nToby placed the rare {{specimen}} on the worktable to measure it. The object had a round shape, with a total {{diameter}} of twenty centimeters, meaning its {{radius}} was exactly ten centimeters. Next, he prepared to test the chemical {{composition}} of the dark stone. He wanted to identify each strange {{substance}} hidden inside it. He knew that rocks on Earth often contained an ancient plant or animal {{fossil}}, but space rocks were completely different.\n\nUsing a laser scanner, Toby examined the rock’s structure. Soon, the screen showed that it contained a rare metallic {{compound}} never formed on our home planet. There was no sign of any biological life or ancient imprint. It was a genuine {{meteorite}} that had survived its fiery fall to the ground. Holding a piece of deep space in his own hands, Toby smiled, knowing he was touching the wonders of the stars without ever leaving Earth.",
    "articleZh": "主题： 仰望星空有助于科学家发现宇宙的奥秘。\n\n托比深夜在高山天文台工作。他从小就梦想成为一名宇航员，前往广袤的宇宙旅行。然而，他最终选择研究真正的科学，成为了一名天文学研究人员。有时朋友们会拿他看星座运势开玩笑，但他总是解释说科学与占星术毫无关系。在托比看来，整个宇宙充满了等待被解开的真正奥秘。\n\n今晚很特别。托比将一台大型望远镜对准漆黑的夜空，观测一颗著名的彗星。当它沿着古老的轨道运行时，正紧贴着黄道面穿过。一层发光的气体和太空尘埃形成的包层包裹着它的头部，拖出一条明亮的尾巴。向更深处望去，托比还能看到远方闪烁着一个遥远的螺旋星系。这是一场真正的天体****奇观，让他的内心充满了惊叹。\n\n突然，他的同事妮娜抱着一个沉重的箱子走进了实验室。她刚从一个干燥的沙漠山谷回来，那里地面上有一个巨大的圆形陨石坑。盒子里装着一块覆盖着灰色灰烬的沉重黑色大块岩石。“我在撞击点附近采集了这个样本，”妮娜兴奋地说，“我们需要检查它是来自深空的星际岩石，还是仅仅是普通的地球石头。”\n\n托比把这个罕见的标本放在工作台上进行测量。该物体呈圆形，总直径为二十厘米，这意味着它的半径正好是十厘米。接下来，他准备测试这块黑色石头的化学成分。他想鉴定隐藏在其中的每一种奇异物质。他知道地球上的岩石通常含有古老的动植物化石，但太空岩石则截然不同。\n\n利用激光扫描仪，托比检查了这块岩石的结构。很快，屏幕显示它含有一种从未在我们的母星上形成过的罕见金属化合物。没有任何生物生命或古老印迹的迹象。这是一颗在灼热坠落到地面后幸存下来的真正陨石。托比手里握着一块来自深空的碎片，露出了微笑，他知道自己无需离开地球，就已经触碰到了群星的奇迹。",
