    "articleEn": "Theme: Even in hard times, the night sky reminds us to keep searching.\n\nMaya worked at a quiet mountain observatory. For months, the small research station had faced serious troubles. A heavy winter storm had damaged the roof, and the town council planned to close the facility for good. Maya felt an {{overwhelming}} pressure to prove the station was still valuable. To her colleagues, the future seemed completely {{hopeless}}, and most of them had already packed their bags and left.\n\nMaya refused to surrender to {{despair}}, even though her time was quickly running out. She was {{desperate}} to find something meaningful before the council made their final decision next week. Every cold evening, she climbed up to the dome and pointed the telescope toward the dark sky. Deep space was filled with countless rocks that were normally {{invisible}} to human eyes, drifting quietly in the cold void.\n\nShe focused her study on ancient space rocks. Millions of years ago, a {{cataclysmic}} disaster had shaken the outer solar system. Two massive bodies had suffered a violent {{collision}}, releasing incredible force into the empty space. That ancient impact had enough power to {{squash}} solid stone into fine dust and fling pieces across millions of miles.\n\nLate one night, a tiny dot moved across her computer screen. At first glance, it was barely {{discernible}} against the pitch-black background. But as Maya carefully sharpened the focus, the faint blur turned into a {{distinct}} trail of bright silver light. A small piece from that ancient event had entered Earth’s atmosphere, blazing like a falling star toward the valley below.\n\nThe next morning, Maya hiked through the snowy woods toward the crash site. In a small hollow of melted ice, she found a dark, glassy stone: a rare meteorite {{fragment}} from that prehistoric impact. Holding the cool rock in her hands, Maya knew the station had a future after all. Disasters could bring terrible loss, but looking up still offered wonder and hope.",
    "articleZh": "主题： 即使在艰难时刻，夜空依然提醒我们保持仰望与探索。\n\n玛雅在一家偏僻的山顶天文台工作。几个月来，这个小型观测站面临着严峻的困难。一场严重的冬季风暴摧毁了屋顶，镇议会甚至计划彻底关闭该设施。玛雅承受着压倒性的巨大压力，必须证明天文台依然具备科学价值。在她的同事们看来，未来似乎完全是无望的，许多人早已收拾行李离开了。\n\n尽管时间所剩无几，玛雅却拒绝向绝望妥协。她急切需要在下周议会做出最终决定之前找到具有重要意义的发现。每个寒冷的夜晚，她都会爬上圆顶，将望远镜对准漆黑的夜空。深空中充满了无数肉眼通常看不见的岩石，它们在冰冷的虚空中静静漂流。\n\n她将研究重点放在古老的太空岩石上。数百万年前，一场剧变的灾难曾震撼整个外太阳系。两个巨大的星体发生了剧烈的碰撞，向空旷的宇宙释放出惊人的能量。那次古老的撞击力量极其巨大，足以将坚硬的岩石压扁成粉末，并将碎屑抛向数百万英里之外。\n\n一天深夜，屏幕上掠过一个小光点。乍看之下，在漆黑的背景中它几乎是不可辨别的。但当玛雅仔细调整焦点时，那道模糊的影子变成了一条明显的银色光轨。原来是一块源自那场古老事件的微小碎石进入了地球大气层，宛如一颗坠落的流星照亮了下方的山谷。\n\n第二天清晨，玛雅徒步穿过雪林走向坠落点。在冰雪融化的小坑中，她找到了一块深色的玻璃质岩石——来自远古撞击的珍贵陨石碎片。把这块冰凉的宇宙碎片握在手中，玛雅知道天文台终于有救了。灾难或许会带来惨痛的打击，但抬头仰望依然能给人带来奇迹与希望。",
