    "articleEn": "Theme: A dedicated teacher helps young learners discover the true joy of school.\n\nLeo believed that good {{education}} could change lives. In his {{primary}} school days and later in {{secondary}} school, he was not always top of the class. He went to a small {{college}} before finishing his degree at a large {{university}}. Back then, he was just a confused {{novice}} who sometimes felt like an {{idiot}} whenever he faced a difficult math {{problem}}. Yet, he worked hard to {{learn}} every day and {{study}} with care to {{acquire}} useful {{knowledge}}.\n\nYears later, Leo began working at a learning {{institute}} connected to a city {{academy}}. Their goal was to {{recruit}} young learners from every background. The leaders treated local schooling as a vital public {{issue}} and not just a private family {{affair}}. They wanted to fight against {{illiteracy}} so that every single child could become fully {{literate}} and {{numerate}}. Some teachers supported {{controversial}} methods; they tried to {{cram}} raw facts into young minds before big tests. Leo disagreed and chose to {{emphasise}} deep understanding instead.\n\nLeo knew that an {{obscure}} math {{puzzle}} or a strange word {{riddle}} could easily scare a beginner. He did not want to {{spoil}} his pupils with cheap rewards or {{indulge}} lazy habits in class. At the same time, he refused to {{abuse}} his power by shouting at them. His real {{motive}} was to {{instil}} a quiet confidence in every student. He used fun stories to {{stimulate}} class discussion and {{motivate}} the quiet children. This created a strong {{impetus}} for independent reading and would {{spur}} their curiosity, which would {{enable}} them to solve new challenges alone.\n\nOne term, a {{clever}} girl named Maya joined the class. She was very {{smart}} and had a natural {{aptitude}} for discovery. Maya was quick with her {{wit}} and always offered funny, thoughtful answers. She was clearly {{intelligent}} and {{capable}} of doing great things, but she needed guidance to become a true {{all-round}} student. Leo wanted to {{enhance}} her skills and help her develop real {{expertise}} over time.\n\nMaya did not think of herself as a rare {{genius}}, nor did she care about joining a wealthy {{elite}}. She just wanted to understand the world. Leo shared his own {{wisdom}} to {{inspire}} her to aim high. With his support, she wrote an {{excellent}} report and gave an {{outstanding}} talk to the school. It was a {{brilliant}} start to the term, reminding everyone that real learning begins with patience and care.",
    "articleZh": "主题： 一位敬业的老师帮助年轻学子发现求学的真正乐趣。\n\n利奥坚信，良好的教育能够改变人生。在小学时代以及后来的中学阶段，他并不总是名列前茅。在进入一所大型大学完成学位之前，他曾就读于一所小型学院。那时，他还只是一个懵懂的新手，每当面对棘手的数学难题时，有时甚至觉得自己像个笨蛋。然而，他每天都努力学习，认真钻研，去获取有用的知识。\n\n多年后，利奥开始在一家附属于一所城市专科院校的研修机构工作。他们的目标是从各种背景中招收年轻学子。领导层将当地办学视为一项至关重要的公共议题，而不仅仅是私人的家庭事务。他们希望消除文盲现象，让每一个孩子都能具备充分的读写能力和计算能力。一些老师支持颇具争议的方法；他们试图在重大考试前将生硬的事实死记硬背地塞进年轻人的大脑中。利奥对此并不认同，而是选择强调深度理解。\n\n利奥深知，一个晦涩难懂的数学难题或一个奇怪的文字谜语很容易吓倒初学者。他不想用廉价的奖励来溺爱学生，也不愿在课堂上纵容懒散的习惯。与此同时，他拒绝通过大声斥责来滥用自己的权力。他真正的动机是在每个学生心中灌输一种沉静的自信。他用有趣的故事来激发课堂讨论，并激励那些沉默寡言的孩子。这为自主阅读创造了强大的动力，并能激起他们的好奇心，从而使他们能够独自应对新的挑战。\n\n有一个学期，一个名叫玛雅的聪慧女孩加入了这个班级。她非常聪明，对探索有着天生的天赋。玛雅机智敏捷，总是能给出风趣且深刻的回答。她显然非常聪敏，并且有能力成就一番大事，但她需要引导才能成为一名真正的全面发展的学生。利奥希望提升她的技能，并帮助她随着时间的推移培养出真正的专长。\n\n玛雅并不认为自己是什么罕见的天才，也对跻身富有的精英阶层毫无兴趣。她只是想了解这个世界。利奥分享了自己的智慧，去启发她树立远大目标。在他的支持下，她写出了一篇优秀的报告，并在全校面前做了一场杰出的演讲。这是新学期一个精彩的开端，它提醒着所有人：真正的学习始于耐心与关爱。",
