    "articleEn": "Theme: A new university student attends orientation and learns about college life.\n\nLeo arrived on the green university {{campus}} on a sunny morning. It was a famous {{coed}} college known for high {{prestige}} and an ancient {{reputation}}. Today was the official {{matriculation}} day. As an excited {{fresher}}, Leo had to {{enrol}} in his courses and {{register}} his name at the front desk. A helpful {{assistant}} checked the student {{roster}} and handed him a temporary parking {{permit}}. After that, Leo walked into the main hall for the morning {{orientation}}.\n\nOn the raised wooden {{platform}}, key leaders of the university stood together. The college {{principal}} stood beside the school {{dean}}. Together, they introduced the entire teaching {{faculty}} to the crowd. An {{eminent}} {{professor}}, who was also a brilliant {{scientist}} and an active {{scholar}}, gave a welcoming speech. He was much friendlier than Leo’s strict high school {{headmaster}}. The older students clearly {{esteem}} the man, and everyone in the room showed deep {{respect}} for his work. Later, a young {{lecturer}} and a personal {{tutor}} also stepped forward to meet their small study groups.\n\nIn the crowd, Leo met an older guide who would act as his student {{mentor}}. This helpful {{senior}} had studied at the college for three years. Beside him were a cheerful {{sophomore}} and a quiet {{junior}}. They explained that success required a {{diligent}} spirit and {{painstaking}} study habits. One science course was {{notorious}} for extremely hard exams, so every student needed a smart study {{scheme}}. “You must build real research {{skill}} and find the right learning {{approach}},” the guide explained. “When you were a young {{pupil}}, teachers gave you every answer, but here you must think for yourself.”\n\nTo {{qualify}} for advanced lab projects, each student had to prove they were a serious {{candidate}}. The university would {{certify}} their progress after each semester. Depending on their goals, students could complete a {{bachelor}}, continue for a {{master}}, or even become a {{doctor}} of philosophy. Certain careers also required a special state {{license}} before someone could work professionally. Leo knew earning such a {{degree}} would take years of dedication.\n\nThe hall walls displayed portraits of famous {{alumni}} who had achieved great things. One honored {{graduate}} had become a brave {{ambassador}} representing the country, while another was a skilled {{diplomat}} working for world peace. At the end of the tour, Leo imagined the day of his own final {{ceremony}}, when he would proudly hold his official {{diploma}}. With confidence in his heart, he was ready to begin his journey.",
    "articleZh": "主题： 一名大学新生参加迎新活动并了解大学生活。\n\n在一个阳光明媚的早晨，利奥来到了绿树成荫的大学校园。这是一所著名的男女同校学院，以崇高的声望和悠久的声誉而闻名。今天是正式的入学日。作为一名兴奋的大学一年级新生，利奥必须选课并在前台登记姓名。一位热心的助手核对了学生名册，并递给他一张临时停车许可证。随后，利奥走进大厅参加上午的迎新培训。\n\n在凸起的木制讲台上，大学的主要领导们站在一起。学院校长站在学院院长身旁。他们一同向众人介绍了全体教学教职员工。一位杰出的****教授发表了欢迎致辞，他同时也是一位才华横溢的科学家和一位活跃的学者。他比利奥高中时那位严厉的校长要和蔼可亲得多。高年级学生显然非常敬重这位长者，在场的每个人都对他的工作表现出深深的尊敬。随后，一位年轻的讲师和一位个人导师也走上前去与他们负责的研讨小组见面。\n\n在人群中，利奥遇到了一位将担任他学生导师的高年级学长。这位乐于助人的大学四年级学生已经在这所学院学习了三年。在他身边，还有一位开朗的大学二年级学生和一位文静的大学三年级学生。他们解释说，取得成功需要勤勉的精神和刻苦的学习习惯。有一门科学课程因极其严苛的考试而声名狼藉，因此每个学生都需要一个聪明的学习计划。“你必须培养真正的研究技能，并找到正确的学习方法，”这位向导解释道，“当你还是个小学生时，老师会把每个答案都给你，但在这里你必须独立思考。”\n\n为了取得资格参与高级实验室项目，每个学生都必须证明自己是一个认真对待学业的候选人。大学会在每个学期后对他们的学业进展进行证明。根据各自的目标，学生可以攻读学士，继续深造获得硕士，甚至成为哲学博士。某些职业在个人从事专业工作之前，还需要获得特殊的国家执照。利奥深知，获得这样一个学位需要多年的全身心投入。\n\n大厅的墙上陈列着功成名就的著名校友们的画像。一位备受赞誉的毕业生成为了代表国家的勇敢大使，而另一位则成为了致力于世界和平的干练外交官。在参观接近尾声时，利奥想象着自己参加最终毕业典礼的那一天，届时他将自豪地手握正式的毕业文凭。怀揣着坚定的信心，他已准备好开启自己的人生新旅程。",
