    "articleEn": "Theme: A student organizes his school term and learns effective study habits.\n\nAt the start of the new {{term}}, Leo sat in his room to organize his university {{semester}}. He logged into the university’s online {{system}} and downloaded the full {{curriculum}}. First, he looked at his weekly {{timetable}} and created a balanced daily {{schedule}}. He had to register for a {{compulsory}} science course, which was a necessary {{prerequisite}} for his second-year classes. The university was very {{selective}} about lab admissions, but Leo also chose a relaxed history {{elective}}. Before classes began, he decided to {{print}} out each course {{syllabus}} so that he knew what to expect.\n\nIn his main science {{course}}, Leo quickly realized that the first {{lesson}} was not simple. The professor warned the students not to stay on the {{surface}} with {{superficial}} thinking, because the subject held {{profound}} ideas about the universe. At first, Leo’s knowledge was only {{rudimentary}} and {{elementary}}. To succeed, he had to master every {{basic}} concept and understand each {{fundamental}} {{principle}}. Instead of learning an old religious {{doctrine}}, the class studied modern scientific {{theory}} and gathered {{empirical}} facts through experiments. Leo really enjoyed this {{practical}} way of learning.\n\nLeo soon discovered that success required good study habits and strong personal {{discipline}}. Before every weekly {{seminar}}, he would {{preview}} the textbook chapters. If he had very little time, he would quickly {{skim}} the main headings and {{scan}} the pages for important keywords. Later in the evening, he would {{scrutinise}} complex data charts and {{inspect}} his lab notes for any errors. Whenever he had questions, he would {{consult}} his teacher or post a question on the student {{forum}}. His professor did not simply {{dictate}} answers for students to {{recite}}; instead, she pushed them to think for themselves.\n\nAs the weeks passed, the first important {{deadline}} approached for a major research {{assignment}}. Leo made sure to {{revise}} his draft carefully before he clicked to {{submit}} it. The tutor reminded everyone never to {{plagiarise}} or {{copy}} someone else’s work. Next, Leo gave a successful group {{presentation}} and scored high marks on a weekly {{quiz}}. To prepare for the final {{examination}}, he took time to {{review}} his flashcards and complete a practice {{test}}. By building good study habits, Leo finished his studies with pride.",
    "articleZh": "主题： 一名学生规划自己的学期并养成高效的学习习惯。\n\n在新学期（学期）伊始，利奥坐在房间里规划他的大学学期（学期）。他登录了大学的网络系统（系统），下载了完整的课程体系（课程体系）。首先，他查看了自己的每周时间表（时间表），并制定了一份均衡的每日日程安排（日程安排）。他必须注册一门科学必修（必修）课，这是他大二课程必不可少的先修课程（先修课程）。大学在实验室录取方面非常严格（挑剔的），但利奥还选修了一门轻松的历史选修课（选修课）。在开课前，他决定打印（打印）出每门课的教学大纲（教学大纲），以便心中有数。\n\n在他的主要科学课程（课程）中，利奥很快意识到第一堂课（课）并不简单。教授告诫学生们不要停留在表面（表面），带着肤浅的（肤浅的）思维，因为这门学科蕴含着关于宇宙的深刻（深刻的）思想。起初，利奥的知识还只是粗浅的（粗浅的）和初级的（初级的）。为了取得好成绩，他必须掌握每一个基础（基础）概念，并理解每一条根本（根本的）原理（原理）。课堂上没有去学习古老的宗教教义（教义），而是研究了现代科学理论（理论），并通过实验收集实证（实证的）事实。利奥非常喜欢这种务实的（实用的）学习方式。\n\n利奥很快发现，成功需要良好的学习习惯和强大的个人自律（自律）。在每周的研讨会（研讨会）之前，他都会预习（预习）课本章节。如果时间非常紧迫，他会快速略读（略读）主要标题，并在页面中扫读（扫读）重要关键词。傍晚时分，他会仔细审视（细审）复杂的数据图表，并检查（检查）实验笔记中是否存在错误。每当有疑问时，他都会请教（请教）老师，或在学生论坛（论坛）上发帖提问。他的教授不会简单地口述（口述）答案让学生们去背诵（背诵）；相反，她推动他们去独立思考。\n\n随着几周过去，一项重要研究作业（作业）的第一个重要截止日期（截止日期）临近了。利奥在点击提交（提交）之前，确保仔细修改（修改）了草稿。导师提醒大家绝不能抄袭（抄袭）或照搬（复制）他人的成果。随后，利奥进行了一次成功的团队展示（展示），并在每周的测验（小测验）中取得了高分。为了准备期末考试（考试），他花时间复习（复习）抽认卡，并完成了一套模拟测试（测试）。通过养成良好的学习习惯，利奥自豪地完成了学业。",
