    "articleEn": "Theme: A university student works hard on research to earn good scores and financial support.\n\nLeo was a university student working hard on his final {{research}} project. He needed to {{achieve}} enough {{credit}} to graduate, but he was worried about paying his next tuition {{fee}}. He hoped to win a college {{scholarship}} or a research {{fellowship}} to support his studies. His partner Maya worked beside him in the lab. Sometimes they {{disagree}} on small points, and their personal views {{differ}} quite often. However, they both wanted to examine the {{diverse}} learning habits of students across the campus.\n\nTo build their study, they chose an {{inductive}} approach. They wanted to start with small facts and look at every little {{detail}} with {{thorough}} attention. For {{example}}, in one specific {{instance}}, a slight {{nuance}} in student answers gave them an unexpected clue. To collect more data, they made a simple {{questionnaire}} to {{survey}} hundreds of classmates. Maya sat quietly in the library to {{observe}} how people studied. Meanwhile, Leo went to the office to {{inquire}} about missing data and submit a technical {{query}} to the campus network team.\n\nThe early findings began to {{confirm}} their central hypothesis. Leo drew neat charts to {{illustrate}} the key points and {{demonstrate}} that silent study rooms led to better focus. Clear patterns began to {{manifest}} in the test numbers, and this helped to {{prove}} that quiet spaces raised productivity. Still, the team had to {{determine}} what to do next. They had to {{decide}} which errors to remove and {{resolve}} any final doubts. “We must not {{underestimate}} the difficulty of writing the final report,” Maya said. “Nor should we {{overestimate}} our speed.”\n\nTheir main ambition was to {{accomplish}} this task on time and {{attain}} an excellent {{score}}. On the day the results came out, students formed a long {{queue}} near the academic office. Leo waited patiently in front of a long {{row}} of computer desks. Every professor took time to {{mark}} the papers carefully. When the board posted each student’s {{grade}} and overall class {{rank}}, Leo saw his name right at the very top.\n\nThe department head arrived to give high {{praise}} to the pair and to {{grant}} them the annual science {{award}}. Leo and Maya were glad to {{appreciate}} the positive {{feedback}} from their teachers. For Leo, this honor felt like the best possible {{reward}}. Winning this valuable {{prize}} meant he had no tuition stress left, and he was eager to {{apply}} his new research methods to future projects.",
    "articleZh": "主题： 一名大学生努力做研究，以取得好成绩并获得资金资助。\n\n利奥是一名大学生，正为他的毕业研究（research）项目刻苦努力。他需要取得（achieve）足够的学分（credit）才能毕业，但他同时也在为支付下一学期的学费（fee）发愁。他希望能获得大学奖学金（scholarship）或研究奖学金（fellowship）来支持自己的学业。他的搭档玛雅在实验室里与他并肩工作。有时他们会在小细节上意见不一（disagree），个人的看法也常常不同（differ）。然而，他们都希望调查全校学生多样化（diverse）的学习习惯。\n\n为了构建这项研究，他们选择了一种归纳（inductive）方法。他们想要从小处着手，带着透彻（thorough）的专注审视每一个细节（detail）。例如（example），在某个具体的例子（instance）中，学生回答中细微的差异（nuance）为他们提供了一个意想不到的线索。为了收集更多数据，他们制作了一份简单的调查问卷（questionnaire），以对数百名同学进行调查（survey）。玛雅静静地坐在图书馆里观察（observe）大家的学习方式。与此同时，利奥前往办公室询问（inquire）缺失的数据，并向校园网络团队提交了一份技术疑问（query）。\n\n早期的发现开始证实（confirm）他们的核心假设。利奥绘制了整洁的图表来阐明（illustrate）要点，并证明（demonstrate）安静的自习室能带来更好的专注力。测试数据中开始显现（manifest）出清晰的规律，这有助于证明（prove）安静的空间能提高效率。尽管如此，团队仍需确定（determine）下一步该做什么。他们必须决定（decide）消除哪些误差，并解决（resolve）最后的任何疑问。“我们绝不能低估（underestimate）撰写最终报告的难度，”玛雅说，“也不应该高估（overestimate）我们的速度。”\n\n他们的主要目标是按时完成（accomplish）这项任务，并获得（attain）优异的分数（score）。公布结果的那一天，学生们在教务办公室附近排起了长队（queue）。利奥在一长排（row）电脑桌前耐心地等待着。每位教授都花时间仔细地为论文打分（mark）。当公告板公布每位学生的成绩（grade）和班级总排名（rank）时，利奥看到自己的名字赫然位列榜首。\n\n系主任前来对两人给予了高度赞扬（praise），并向他们颁发（grant）了年度科学奖（award）。利奥和玛雅很高兴能够感激（appreciate）来自老师们积极的反馈（feedback）。对利奥而言，这份荣誉感觉就像是所能得到的最好回报（reward）。赢得这项宝贵的奖项（prize）意味着他不再有学费压力，并且他渴望将自己的新研究方法应用（apply）于未来的项目中。",
