    "articleEn": "Theme: A technician works with old and new machines in a school workshop.\n\nLeo works at a school technology {{facility}}. As a child, he loved reading {{science fiction}} books and dreaming of helpful robots. Today, his job is to {{gather}} broken machines and {{assemble}} them again. He uses every hand {{tool}} and piece of modern {{equipment}} on his workbench. On one side sits a kitchen {{appliance}} waiting for repair, right next to an electric musical {{instrument}}. Leo believes that every small {{device}} must {{belong}} in an orderly room.\n\nLeo sits down with his {{laptop}} and connects to the school {{network}}. He opens an internet {{browser}} to download update {{software}} for an experimental {{microcomputer}}. He types quickly on the {{keyboard}} and watches the bright, {{high-definition}} {{screen}}. Nearby, an old test telephone rings. He must {{dial}} a number to check the line, listening carefully through the receiver.\n\nNext, Leo tests a sound system. He finds an old music {{cassette}} and fixes it with plastic {{tape}}. Then he speaks into a {{microphone}} and listens to the clear {{audio}} coming from a large {{loudspeaker}}. Years ago, sound was stored on physical reels, but now everything uses {{binary}} numbers in a {{digital}} format, sent through a {{wireless}} signal.\n\nLeo also loves the field of {{optics}}. He cleans the curved glass {{lens}} on a desktop {{microscope}} to ensure sharp {{vision}} for the science students. After that, he checks a mini {{radar}} and a motion {{sensor}}. When the machine beeps, the sound produces a sharp {{echo}} off the concrete wall.\n\nNow, it is time to check numbers. Leo will {{measure}} the electric current and read the pressure {{gauge}}. He must {{calculate}} the power level, run a fast {{compute}} task, and {{count}} the spare parts in a box. After doing that, he will {{estimate}} the total cost, {{assess}} the safety risks, and {{evaluate}} whether the unit is ready to go back to the classroom.\n\nFinally, Leo picks up a useful {{accessory}}: a small, {{auxiliary}} power cable that makes the station truly {{versatile}}. Heat was an unwanted {{byproduct}} of the processor, so he decides to {{add}} a silent cooling fan so dust does not {{accumulate}}. He will {{attach}} a green sticker to finish the project. Turning this old workshop into a modern {{multimedia}} center once felt like an impossible {{fantasy}}, but now it is completely real.",
    "articleZh": "主题： 一名技术人员在学校车间里摆弄新旧机器。\n\n利奥在一家学校科技设施工作。孩提时代，他喜欢阅读科幻书籍，梦想着拥有能提供帮助的机器人。今天，他的工作是收集损坏的机器并重新组装它们。他用遍了工作台上的每一件手持工具和现代设备。一侧放着一台等待维修的厨房器具，紧挨着一件电子乐器。利奥认为，每一个小装置都必须归放在一个井井有条的房间里。\n\n利奥带着他的笔记本电脑坐下，并连接到学校网络。他打开互联网浏览器，为一台实验性微型计算机下载更新软件。他在键盘上快速敲击，注视着明亮的高清晰度****屏幕。在附近，一部旧的测试电话响了起来。他必须拨打一个号码来检查线路，通过听筒仔细聆听。\n\n接下来，利奥测试了一套音响系统。他找到一盘旧音乐磁带，并用塑料胶带将其修复。然后他对着麦克风讲话，聆听从大型扬声器中传出的清晰音频。多年前，声音存储在实体卷盘上，但现在一切都使用数字格式的二进制数字，通过无线信号发送。\n\n利奥还热爱光学领域。他清理了一台台式显微镜上的曲面玻璃透镜，以确保理科学生能拥有清晰的视野。之后，他检查了一台微型雷达和一个运动传感器。当机器发出哔哔声时，声音在混凝土墙上产生了清脆的回声。\n\n现在，是核对数字的时候了。利奥将测量电流并读取压力仪表。他必须计算功率水平，运行一个快速的计算任务，并清点盒子里备用零件的数量。完成这些后，他将估算总成本，评估安全风险，并评估该设备是否已准备好送回教室。\n\n最后，利奥拿起了一件有用的配件：一根小型的辅助电源线，它使这个工作台变得真正多功能。热量是处理器产生的不受欢迎的副产品，因此他决定添加一个静音冷却风扇，以免灰尘积聚。他将贴上一张绿色贴纸来完成这个项目。把这个旧车间变成一个现代化的多媒体中心曾经感觉是一个不可能实现的幻想，但现在它完全成为了现实。",
