    "articleEn": "Theme: Engineers improve a water cleaning machine in a factory.\n\nLeo worked at an old water treatment plant near the city river. His team wanted to build a new {{prototype}} machine to {{purify}} dirty river water and manage {{sewage}}. The strong steel {{framework}} of the machine stood in the main hall. A loud {{generator}} provided electricity, and a large metal {{pump}} pushed water through thick pipes. Good {{ventilation}} kept fresh air moving inside the hot room. Leo was in charge of the first test {{phase}}.\n\nLeo watched how each mechanical {{aspect}} worked together. He checked the big {{gear}} and the metal {{pivot}} that allowed the heavy arm to turn smoothly. A strong {{hydraulic}} press pushed down to {{compress}} wet waste into solid blocks, which would {{facilitate}} quick cleaning later. Soon, the machine began to {{operate}} in normal {{mode}}. A screen helped {{filter}} stones from the liquid. Next, hot steam rose so it could {{condense}} on cold plates to {{distil}} clean water.\n\nHowever, under this test {{circumstance}}, something went {{wrong}}. Dirty water suddenly spilled on the floor because the underground {{drainage}} line was blocked. Leo began to {{stumble}} in the dark corner as red warning lights flashed. There was an obvious mechanical {{fault}} in the system. Leo knew he must not make another careless {{mistake}}. He needed to find the exact {{error}} that caused this trouble and see if there was a hidden {{flaw}} in the pipes.\n\nLeo used a small light to {{pinpoint}} the leak behind the main tank. His first measurement was not {{accurate}}, so he took a more {{precise}} reading with a digital tool. He found that a rubber ring was missing. To {{correct}} the problem, he had to {{alter}} the pipe joint and {{adjust}} the pressure valve. He also had to {{mould}} a soft plastic ring by hand to seal the gap. Leo decided to {{simplify}} the pipe layout so workers could repair it easily in the future.\n\nThe team prepared for every possible {{contingency}} before restarting the engine. During the night {{shift}}, it was Leo’s {{turn}} to watch the control panel. He decided to {{adapt}} the engine so it could {{convert}} waste heat into extra power. This idea helped {{refine}} the whole process and {{transform}} the old workshop into a modern station. Finally, the team was ready to {{shift}} into full production with complete success.",
    "articleZh": "主题： 工程师们在一家工厂里改进了一台净水机。\n\n利奥在城市河流附近的一家老旧污水处理厂工作。他的团队想要制造一台新的原型机，以净化肮脏的河水并处理污水。机器坚固的钢制框架立在大厅里。一台发出巨响的发电机提供电力，一台大型金属泵推动水穿过粗粗的管道。良好的通风使新鲜空气在闷热的房间里保持流动。利奥负责第一测试阶段。\n\n利奥观察着每个机械方面是如何协同工作的。他检查了大齿轮以及使重臂平稳转动的金属支点。一台强劲的液压机向下按压，把湿废料压缩成实心块，这将有助于促进随后快速的清理工作。很快，机器开始在正常模式下运转。一块滤网帮助从液体中过滤掉石头。接着，热蒸汽上升，以便在冷板上凝结，从而蒸馏出清水。\n\n然而，在这种测试情况下，出了差错。由于地下排水管线堵塞，脏水突然溅落到地板上。随着红色警报灯闪烁，利奥在黑暗的角落里开始踉跄绊倒。系统中存在一处明显的机械故障。利奥知道自己绝不能再犯粗心的过失。他需要找出引发这一麻烦的确切错误，并查看管道中是否存在隐蔽的缺陷。\n\n利奥用一盏小灯精准定位了主水箱后面的泄漏点。他的第一次测量并不准确，于是他用数字工具进行了更精确的读数。他发现少了一个橡胶圈。为了纠正这个问题，他不得不改动管道接头并调整压力阀。他还必须亲手浇铸成型一个软塑料环来密封缝隙。利奥决定简化管道布局，以便工人们将来能够轻松维修。\n\n在重新启动引擎之前，团队为每一种可能的突发情况做好了准备。在夜班期间，轮到利奥看守控制面板了。他决定改造引擎，使其能够将废热转换为额外的动力。这个想法有助于完善整个工艺流程，并将老旧的车间改造为一个现代化的工作站。最终，团队准备好完全转向全面生产，取得了圆满成功。",
