    "articleEn": "Theme: Clear communication helps people solve disagreements and work together.\n\nElena worked at a youth center in Oxford. Her main job was to help international students {{communicate}} without fear. On Monday morning, twenty students from six different countries gathered in the hall for a community challenge. Before the session started, Elena had to {{translate}} a welcome letter for the new arrivals. She also needed to {{decipher}} some messy handwritten notes left on the whiteboard by the previous teacher.\n\nSoon, the students sat around a large wooden table for a lively {{discussion}}. Their task was to {{brainstorm}} fresh ideas to protect the local river. At first, everyone smiled and shared simple suggestions. However, a sharp {{contention}} soon arose between two group leaders, Marcus and Kenji, about how much money they should spend on cleaning equipment.\n\nThe disagreement quickly turned into an intense {{debate}}. Kenji spoke very quickly in his native language when he got excited, so Elena stepped in to {{interpret}} his thoughts into English. When some statements sounded too aggressive, Elena chose to {{paraphrase}} the core messages using softer sentences. This helped the group focus on practical solutions instead of hurt feelings.\n\nMarcus was a confident speaker, and his natural {{eloquence}} held everyone’s attention. Yet, fancy words alone were not enough to solve the problem. Elena drew a simple diagram on the board to {{illuminate}} the cost differences between the two proposals. Then, to bring the group closer, she invited Kenji to {{narrate}} a story about a river cleanup in his own hometown.\n\nTheir teacher watched from the back of the room and offered a positive {{commentary}}, praising how patiently the students listened. Hearing Kenji’s story helped Marcus realize that both teams wanted the exact same goal. The two leaders sat down together to {{negotiate}} a balanced budget that satisfied everyone. By late afternoon, the room was filled with smiles, and their joint project was ready.",
    "articleZh": "主题： 清晰的沟通有助于人们化解分歧、携手合作。\n\n埃琳娜在牛津的一家青年中心工作。她的主要任务是帮助国际学生毫无畏惧地进行交流。周一上午，来自六个不同国家的二十名学生聚集在大厅，准备参加一项社区挑战赛。在活动开始前，埃琳娜必须为刚到的新生翻译一封欢迎信。她还需要破译前一位老师留在白板上的一些潦草的手写笔记。\n\n很快，学生们围坐在一张大木桌旁，展开了热烈的讨论。他们的任务是集思广益，为保护当地的河流想出新点子。起初，大家面带微笑，分享着简单的建议。然而，两位组长马库斯和健司之间很快就购买清洁设备的花费产生了激烈的争论。\n\n分歧迅速演变成了一场激烈的辩论。健司激动时语速飞快地讲着自己的母语，于是埃琳娜介入进来，将他的想法口译成英语。当某些发言听起来过于激进时，埃琳娜选择用更柔和的句子来意译核心信息。这帮助团队将注意力集中在切实的解决方案上，而不是受挫的情绪中。\n\n马库斯是一个自信的发言者，他与生俱来的雄辩口才吸引了所有人的注意力。然而，仅靠华丽的辞藻并不足以解决问题。埃琳娜在白板上画了一个简单的图表，以阐明两份提案之间的成本差异。随后，为了拉近大家的距离，她邀请健司讲述一个关于在他家乡清理河流的故事。\n\n他们的老师在教室后方观察着，并给予了积极的评价，称赞学生们倾听时展现出的耐心。听了健司的故事后，马库斯意识到两个小组的目标其实完全一致。两位组长坐在一起，共同协商出一个让所有人都满意的平衡预算。傍晚时分，房间里充满了笑容，他们的联合项目也准备就绪了。",
