    "articleEn": "Theme: Artists and musicians prepare a community festival combining pictures and songs.\n\nLeo was a young {{artist}} who worked hard for his first big {{exhibition}} at the town {{gallery}}. As a creative {{painter}}, he would often {{draw}} the market in the morning and make a pencil {{sketch}} of passing birds. His good friend Marco was a patient {{craftsman}}. Marco liked to {{carve}} soft wood to shape a lovely {{sculpture}} of a horse. Marco also used an old family {{photograph}} to help Leo create a detailed {{portrait}} of his grandfather. Together, they wanted to {{depict}} a quiet morning {{scene}} and {{describe}} their peaceful village to visitors.\n\nThe two friends needed to {{select}} their best work for the show. Their shared {{aesthetic}} idea was to connect images with sounds. Therefore, they decided to {{opt}} for a mixed arts night. Marco loved to {{collect}} classic records, so he placed an old music {{disc}} by the entrance. Leo believed every artwork had a special {{role}} to play, especially his large colorful {{painting}} near the window. The room quickly took on a warm, {{musical}} atmosphere.\n\nRight next to the art hall, workers built a wooden {{stage}} for the evening performance. A local youth {{band}} was excited to perform. They knew their audience liked many styles, from formal {{classical}} pieces and smooth {{jazz}} to energetic {{rock}}, modern {{hip-hop}}, and simple catchy {{pop}}. The singer took time to write a poetic {{lyric}} on a piece of paper to remember every word.\n\nBefore the show started, the players carried their instruments onto the platform. A black grand {{piano}} stood beside an elegant wooden {{violin}} and a deep, heavy {{cello}}. A girl warmed up her silver {{flute}}, and a boy cleaned the brass mouthpiece of his bright {{trumpet}}. Near them, a tall musician held a brown acoustic {{guitar}}, while the beat-maker tapped lightly on a large bass {{drum}}. The singer pulled a pocket {{harmonica}} from his jacket, ready to add some blues feeling.\n\nSoon, the event began. The players needed to {{tune}} their instruments to make sure every note was accurate. As they played, each instrument produced a clear, sweet {{tone}}. When the main song ended, they decided to {{improvise}} together without any sheet music. The guitarist stepped forward to deliver an inspiring {{solo}}. A bright {{melody}} danced over the room, driven by a steady {{rhythm}} that got everyone tapping their feet. The paintings on the walls seemed to shine brighter with every chord.",
    "articleZh": "主题： 艺术家和音乐家筹备一场结合图画与歌曲的社区节日活动。\n\n利奥是一位年轻的艺术家，正为自己在镇美术馆的首次大型展览而努力准备。作为一名富有创造力的画家，他常常在清晨画下集市的景象，并用铅笔素描飞过的鸟儿。他的好朋友马可是一位有耐心的手艺人。马可喜欢雕刻软木，塑出一匹可爱骏马的雕像。马可还用了一张旧的家庭照片，协助利奥创作了一幅细致的祖父肖像画。他们希望共同描摹出一个宁静的清晨场景，并向参观者描绘他们祥和的村庄。\n\n这两位朋友需要为展览挑选出他们最好的作品。他们共同的美学理念是将图像与声音联系起来。因此，他们决定选择举办一个综合艺术之夜。马可喜欢收集经典唱片，所以他在入口处放置了一张老音乐唱片。利奥相信每件艺术品都扮演着特殊的角色，尤其是他靠近窗户的那幅色彩斑斓的大幅画作。整个房间很快充满了温馨且富于音乐感的氛围。\n\n就在艺术厅隔壁，工人们为晚间的演出搭建了一个木质舞台。当地的一支青年乐队对这次演出充满期待。他们知道观众喜欢多种风格，从庄重的古典乐篇章、流畅的爵士乐，到充满活力的摇滚乐、现代的嘻哈乐，以及简单动听的流行音乐。歌手特意花时间在一张纸上写下了富有诗意的歌词，以记住每一个字词。\n\n演出开始前，乐手们将乐器搬上了台。一架黑色大钢琴立在一把优雅的木质小提琴和一把低沉厚重的大提琴身旁。一个女孩正在给她的银色长笛热身，而一个男孩正在清洁他那明亮小号的黄铜吹嘴。在他们附近，一位高个子音乐家抱着一把棕色原声吉他，而负责节奏的人则轻轻敲击着一个巨大的低音鼓。歌手从夹克里掏出一支袖珍口琴，准备添上几分蓝调的韵味。\n\n不久，活动开始了。演奏者们需要给乐器调音，以确保每一个音符都精准无误。随着他们的演奏，每件乐器都发出了清澈悦耳的音色。当主歌结束时，他们决定在没有乐谱的情况下一起即兴演奏。吉他手走上前，带来了一段鼓舞人心的独奏。明快的旋律在房间上方飞扬，伴随着稳健的节奏，让在场的每个人都不由自主地跟着跺起脚来。墙上的画作在每一个和弦的映衬下，似乎都显得更加熠熠生辉。",
