    "articleEn": "Theme: A young man cleans and organizes his cluttered home.\n\nLeo looked around his small flat and sighed. There was too much {{stuff}} everywhere. He had to pack for a move and sort every single {{item}} in each room. Over the years, he had bought colourful {{merchandise}} at concerts, kept a small wooden {{souvenir}} from every trip, and even found a stone {{artifact}} at an old village market. In his study, he noticed bags of {{raw}} wool and other craft {{material}} that he had never touched. On his shelf, a {{crude}} handmade pot sat next to a silver kitchen {{utensil}}. He realized that only a few things were a true {{necessity}}.\n\nLeo decided to separate his things into piles. He did not want to create extra {{waste}} or send useful items to a local {{landfill}}. Many old cardboard boxes were just broken {{junk}}. Still, he could {{recycle}} old paper and plastic bottles, and he chose to {{reuse}} strong glass jars for food storage. The real dirt had to go outside: spoiled food went into the kitchen {{garbage}}, torn papers were thrown out as regular {{rubbish}}, and broken toys were dropped into the main {{trash}} bin. In the hallway, he also picked up wind-blown {{litter}} near the front door.\n\nNext, Leo went into the bathroom. He put on an old working {{outfit}} to protect his clothes and opened his cleaning {{kit}}. The room had a few small problems. Under the sink, a metal {{pipe}} was dripping water, and the building {{sewerage}} smelled a bit unpleasant. When he turned the water {{tap}}, water began filling the big bath {{tub}} because the drain {{plug}} was firmly stuck. He quickly pulled it free so the water could flow away.\n\nLeo then arranged his toiletries neatly. He found an empty bottle of hair {{shampoo}}, a wet bar of body {{soap}}, and a squeeze {{tube}} of hand {{lotion}}. After throwing away the empty bottles, he poured some strong {{detergent}} into a bucket of warm water. He scrubbed the sink and the walls until everything was clean and bright.\n\nFinally, it was time to finish the dusty floors. Leo took his wooden {{broom}} to {{sweep}} dust from every corner of the bedroom and living room. Then, he dipped his {{mop}} into the soapy bucket and washed the kitchen tiles. When the hard work was complete, his flat smelled fresh, looked tidy, and felt like home again.",
    "articleZh": "主题： 一个年轻人打扫并整理凌乱的家。\n\n利奥环顾着自己的小公寓，叹了口气。到处都是太多的东西。他必须为搬家打包，并整理每个房间里的每一样物品。这些年来，他在音乐会上买过色彩鲜艳的周边商品，每次旅行都会留一件小木制纪念品，甚至还在一个古老村落的集市上淘到过一件石制手工艺品。在书房里，他注意到几袋从未碰过的原料羊毛和其他手工艺材料。在架子上，一个粗糙的手工罐子放在一件银质厨房用具旁边。他意识到，只有很少的几样东西才是真正的必需品。\n\n利奥决定把他的东西分堆整理。他不想制造多余的废物，也不想把有用的东西送到当地的垃圾填埋场。许多旧纸箱纯粹是破损的废旧杂物。不过，他可以回收利用旧纸张和塑料瓶，并且他选择重新利用结实的玻璃罐来存放食物。真正的脏东西必须扔到外面去：变质的食物扔进了厨房的厨余垃圾桶，碎纸片作为普通垃圾扔掉，破损的玩具则被扔进了主垃圾箱。在走廊里，他还捡起了前门附近被风吹来的零星垃圾。\n\n接下来，利奥走进了浴室。他穿上一套旧的工作服装以保护里面的衣服，并打开了他的清洁工具箱。这个房间有几个小问题。水槽下方，一根金属水管正在滴水，大楼的排水系统闻起来有点难闻。当他拧开水龙头时，水开始注满大浴缸，因为排水塞被卡得严严实实。他赶紧把它拔出来，好让水流走。\n\n利奥接着把洗漱用品摆放整齐。他发现了一个空的洗发水瓶，一块湿漉漉的香皂，还有一管挤压式的护手乳液。扔掉空瓶后，他把一些强效清洁剂倒进了一桶温水里。他擦洗了水槽和墙壁，直到所有东西都变得干净明亮。\n\n最后，到了清理布满灰尘的地板的时候了。利奥拿起他的木扫帚，清扫卧室和客厅每个角落的灰尘。然后，他把拖把浸入肥皂水桶中，清洗了厨房的瓷砖。当繁重的家务完成后，他的公寓闻起来清新怡人，看起来整洁有序，又有了家的感觉。",
